es"],"notes":"Its end is the month of the Railroad Commission's order (decision 17), effective the day it was signed; the last run isn't dated. Much of the grade is a fire road today, the Old Railroad Grade.","geometry_confidence":"surveyed","geometry_method":"OpenHistoricalMap way 200221495 (CC0, as of 2026-10-16), which OHM's mappers drew from USGS Tamalpais 1897 topographic map, cut from -122.54810,37.90650; checked on USGS Tamalpais 1:62,500 (1941) and USGS Tamalpais 1:62,500 (1897). Cut at the Mill Valley depot (today's Depot Plaza, Throckmorton and Miller Aves), where the way joins the Northwestern Pacific's Mill Valley branch; drawn from the 15-minute sheet, so the switchbacks of the Double Bow Knot are simplified. Up Blithedale Canyon it follows today's West Blithedale Ave, as the railroad did; the 1897 sheet itself draws the canyon about 150 m west of where it is, and the 1941 sheet draws the old grade as a road."}}
